  "entry": {
    "title": "v1 -- The building blocks of context: metadata, semantic layer, ontology, and knowledge graph",
    "url": "/blog/the-building-blocks-of-context-metadata-semantic-layer-ontology-and-knowledge-graph",
    "lead_paragraph": {
      "type": "doc",
      "attrs": {},
      "uid": "8f76dd251d3849f189032915629d1522",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": ""
        }
      ],
      "_version": 1
    },
    "content": [
      {
        "text": {
          "text_content": {
            "type": "doc",
            "attrs": {},
            "uid": "8333c1bb1fdd4329b7fd63a91a74e340",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "h3",
                "uid": "252f097e5b1241be954c5cf28ee3e7e8",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Quick Answer",
                    "attrs": {
                      "style": {
                        "color": "rgb(26, 78, 159)"
                      }
                    },
                    "bold": true,
                    "font-color": "#fa660f"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "ul",
                "uid": "b6047ff3b4dc4456be3525c8ac5b0599",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "li",
                    "uid": "e3ae760d76054aeda430f717304d1ccd",
                    "attrs": {},
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "type": "p",
                        "uid": "32ff6e4b99f84e948dcf8bc5f71c14b9",
                        "attrs": {},
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": "A context layer assembles business meaning at the moment a question is asked"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "li",
                    "uid": "79b15453bf814dc9b60fb533aa500124",
                    "attrs": {},
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "type": "p",
                        "uid": "023e248387134f6faefb02313e58793f",
                        "attrs": {},
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": "It combines metadata, business definitions, and relationships so AI understands what your data means at your organization, not just that it exists"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "li",
                    "uid": "5e445e632ecb428e9f62fa0da28ddf2d",
                    "attrs": {},
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "type": "p",
                        "uid": "2c270a05f060413cbd859ba64cb0f955",
                        "attrs": {},
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": "Without one, AI guesses at your business logic. The guess is often wrong."
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "li",
                    "uid": "ad3ded78b197433a95f723500e2e92a5",
                    "attrs": {},
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "type": "p",
                        "uid": "6ed7ffee9dfc44848b063594276bcb64",
                        "attrs": {},
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": "Strategy Mosaic is the governed semantic layer that makes AI answers consistent, accurate, and trustworthy"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "_version": 1
          },
          "_metadata": {
            "uid": "cs68af64e8cf0dbb97"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "text": {
          "text_content": {
            "type": "doc",
            "attrs": {},
            "uid": "f544baef9dbb4a9b98e7da38ba11874e",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "0e6dc635c8c046aaaa5bb5707bf994c7",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Metadata, semantic layer, ontology, knowledge graph, and context layer. These terms are moving from data engineering conversations into executive meetings, and they almost never get defined with any precision, or in a way that everyone can understand."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "faf7714e00ef42e88212a9a4c2701cb2",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "To explain what goes into building context, let's imagine we work at a large video streaming platform. Our goal is to decide whether to renew our latest hit series, Night Market. We'll build each layer and follow it through to the moment an executive gets a governed answer in seconds."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "_version": 1
          },
          "_metadata": {
            "uid": "cs8df717cd81bdb6c5"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "text": {
          "text_content": {
            "type": "doc",
            "attrs": {},
            "uid": "54404e4362404503979a7bf7a85f5cc1",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "fba2f8f354154e8daf478d031a8dcba7",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "[IMAGE PLACEHOLDER]",
                    "bold": true
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "f394fd9e33774b2d9470df32a25ff1fd",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Upload asset to Contentstack and replace this placeholder — source: image_0.png"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "_version": 1
          },
          "_metadata": {
            "uid": "csa10b5cfcae8fbeb8"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "section_anchor": {
          "header_text": "Metadata: data about data",
          "_metadata": {
            "uid": "csc876a26ce158254b"
          },
          "section_id": "metadata-data-about-data"
        }
      },
      {
        "text": {
          "text_content": {
            "type": "doc",
            "attrs": {},
            "uid": "676c1573f36d4fe2b98d13f76a4c1954",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "5c54f0ee11d847038804b2bd5f926485",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "When the Night Market show dropped on the platform, it came with a show ID, episode count, genre, release date, and production cost. None of that tells you whether to renew it. All of it describes the show. That's metadata."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "163d6ec444aa4b53a95693ee3de47e13",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "In enterprise data, metadata works the same way. A column called completion_pct has metadata that describes it: what it measures (the percentage of viewers who watched to the end of an episode), who owns it (the data engineering team), how often it refreshes, and what quality checks it has passed."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "5b65dfea2e3540cea12582784df71762",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Metadata makes data findable, governable, and trustworthy. But knowing a metric exists and knowing what it means to your business are different things."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "_version": 1
          },
          "_metadata": {
            "uid": "cs7a0db7211ea02d40"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "text": {
          "text_content": {
            "type": "doc",
            "attrs": {},
            "uid": "586dcf217adc488ea30c7edd99ca5003",
