      {
        "section_anchor": {
          "header_text": "The semantic layer: what data means",
          "_metadata": {
            "uid": "cs952073b9df44444d"
          },
          "section_id": "the-semantic-layer-what-data-means"
        }
      },
      {
        "text": {
          "text_content": {
            "type": "doc",
            "attrs": {},
            "uid": "328c003d0ff044e2ad1d0532ce704b62",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "2d325763ebeb4c899e16cd453bd4c353",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Metadata tells you what data exists and how it is managed. For example, Night Market has an 87% viewer completion rate. That value is data. Its field name, definition, owner, refresh schedule, lineage, and quality status are metadata."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "c32fefb5f169486f8caf0132eaa07436",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "A semantic layer goes further by defining what that data means to the business and how it should be used to answer questions."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "7364f9290fd54ef0987336e3e93c5493",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "At our streaming platform, \"renewal candidate\" isn't just a phrase, it's a governed definition built on explicit rules:"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "ul",
                "uid": "3aac43f0aca94098bb0e064306f69b7f",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "li",
                    "uid": "1597328aa3874551b4a5021c0d2fcfa0",
                    "attrs": {},
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "type": "p",
                        "uid": "3ecd86c7d4a443e68a35ffcc281a0d1f",
                        "attrs": {},
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": "Completion rate: Above 80%"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "li",
                    "uid": "577e271c279e4696bec58bfe30d3c6c3",
                    "attrs": {},
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "type": "p",
                        "uid": "1bcd6deb1485411caea287b3b1932eb7",
                        "attrs": {},
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": "New subscriber acquisition: Above 10,000 per season"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "li",
                    "uid": "261647963b3e43f6ae7ca04e6c10b7b9",
                    "attrs": {},
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "type": "p",
                        "uid": "df4df50091d64816bd36a37c2416f5a5",
                        "attrs": {},
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": "Production ROI: Net positive"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "598f392e08ad4373a3865169476b9582",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Those rules live in the semantic layer so everyone, analysts, dashboards, AI agents, use the same definition when the question gets asked."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "cf03838e740441c6bedad2058b623c78",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "a",
                    "uid": "00f40bdc0cd346129788c2eb0a1f3e7c",
                    "attrs": {
                      "url": "https://www.strategy.com/software/blog/semantic-layer-for-ai-metadata-is-not-meaning",
                      "target": "_blank"
                    },
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "A data catalog"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " documents the completion rate field. A semantic layer makes sure everyone calculates what \"renewal candidate\" means the same way."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "_version": 1
          },
          "_metadata": {
            "uid": "csefd92b9d8e76d7fa"
          }
        }
      },
