      {
        "section_anchor": {
          "header_text": "Now we can define context",
          "_metadata": {
            "uid": "cs82213dc534844983"
          },
          "section_id": "now-we-can-define-context"
        }
      },
      {
        "text": {
          "text_content": {
            "type": "doc",
            "attrs": {},
            "uid": "01f2727432924c838d287dc36ea76587",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "977740ad51e941cfbad950fc75ae35a1",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Context is the situational awareness that sits on top of everything else."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "131d22ef0313476a8293b622f29954a7",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Here's what it looks like in practice. A VP of Content asks Monday morning, the week after Night Market's season finale: \"Do we greenlight Season 2?\""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "a83820aa0fc14ab0bd83cb90c5e0eaee",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "To answer that correctly, the system assembles:"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "ul",
                "uid": "3be0cbcb6bd6410897a6cffc1d14d57a",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "li",
                    "uid": "95c2989defb943d28ebc3a34d7958f66",
                    "attrs": {},
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "type": "p",
                        "uid": "6f1e7ee39eb345eca391c8d15469221f",
                        "attrs": {},
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": "The content calendar: greenlight window closes in 30 days, Q4 2027 slate has an open slot"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "li",
                    "uid": "738402f54c094eb0a2f1c6e115c0ed5e",
                    "attrs": {},
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "type": "p",
                        "uid": "5759855219c04e90a2d4d9061ed8e74f",
                        "attrs": {},
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": "The semantic definition: renewal threshold = retention impact above 8K new subs, completion rate above 75%, production ROI positive"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "li",
                    "uid": "006008f0828d44ff86691dd712ba0ce8",
                    "attrs": {},
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "type": "p",
                        "uid": "cd8d4dfaf67f407d92d9abf2bd76402b",
                        "attrs": {},
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": "Her role and permissions: VP Content, greenlight authority up to $6M budget"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "li",
                    "uid": "c507be1cac224694aca9caae0096346a",
                    "attrs": {},
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "type": "p",
                        "uid": "5fbc6a4246ba418e928547f658268a3c",
                        "attrs": {},
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": "Live signals: 12K new subs, 87% completion, $4M cost, estimated $6.2M revenue impact"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "e3be6f27f90246e385fc0fd8cea2a1a3",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The answer: \"Night Market meets all renewal thresholds. Estimated Season 2 ROI positive at $6M budget. Q4 2027 slate has a gap. Greenlight recommended.\""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "295eea53a9e64e4c98469e18d0edb839",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The context layer doesn't store this. It assembles the right answer for the right person at the right moment."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "3438b808a48d467e9ab5bcfcd53e74a5",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Metadata tells you the completion rate exists. The semantic layer tells you what \"retention impact\" means at your company. The ontology maps Night Market to its subscribers, its budget, its slate window. The knowledge graph holds the live numbers. The context layer pulls it together on demand."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "70b475f5bb5d4ba9a84480e09f760c65",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "As my colleague Henry described, a "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "a",
                    "uid": "e9876bd76e0541cdafa865a5e217a6a3",
                    "attrs": {
                      "url": "https://software.strategy.com/blog/the-semantic-layer-is-becoming-context-infrastructure-for-ai",
                      "target": "_blank"
                    },
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "context layer"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is the governed system that combines business definitions, relationships, and real-time signals so that AI and analytics tools can reason about your data the way your organization does, not the way a model guesses."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "_version": 1
          },
          "_metadata": {
            "uid": "cs4dfd9f443fafeb45"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "section_anchor": {
          "header_text": "Do enterprises need all five?",
          "_metadata": {
            "uid": "cs2d8bf016c4b1e152"
          },
          "section_id": "do-enterprises-need-all-five"
        }
      },
      {
        "text": {
          "text_content": {
            "type": "doc",
            "attrs": {},
            "uid": "82d0159fc031430dbf94bae36b5ac145",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "30c9623656d94c248e2c8af6d787dd59",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Not as five separate products. Several layers describe and connect your world. The semantic layer settles what the business means."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "2f848b204d064e64a8357db1ef2e5de9",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Metadata can tell you the completion-rate field exists. An ontology can map Night Market to its subscribers, budget, and content slate. A knowledge graph can connect the live facts, while the context layer brings the right information together for the right person at the right moment."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "39cb940665d943ccbdc385c08effa434",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "But none of those capabilities can reliably produce a trusted answer if \"renewal candidate\" means 80% completion in one meeting and 75% in the next. The semantic layer establishes the approved definition and applies it consistently. The final answer is only as trustworthy as the business logic behind it."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "_version": 1
          },
          "_metadata": {
            "uid": "cse8094fe7d165f810"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "section_anchor": {
          "header_text": "Where Strategy Mosaic fits",
          "_metadata": {
            "uid": "csa2fe7d83d4d794aa"
          },
          "section_id": "where-strategy-mosaic-fits"
        }
      },
      {
        "text": {
          "text_content": {
            "type": "doc",
            "attrs": {},
            "uid": "910d629b8dc640b5b3333d9ef8dc357d",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "1624f86a7d484a6db48b5f72feda672e",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Metadata tells AI where the data lives. An ontology tells it how the business is connected. A knowledge graph provides the facts. But someone still has to apply your company's definitions before an answer is generated."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "a1a4615e13ca4b75a55ae56f294e93eb",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "That's the job of the semantic layer and where "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "a",
                    "uid": "563a56bd66b24349afeb5404f0c812dd",
                    "attrs": {
                      "url": "https://www.strategy.com/software/strategymosaic",
                      "target": "_blank"
                    },
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "Strategy Mosaic"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " fits."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "1f091b319c1840b58d54a05ac9b82c92",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Mosaic is the layer where your business definitions live, where metrics are calculated consistently, and where AI queries get answered deterministically rather than inferred. Most AI tools try to guide the LLM to a better answer. Mosaic takes a different approach: the LLM handles natural language, Mosaic handles the actual data request, applying your business definitions before a single row is read. In head-to-head testing, direct LLM-to-database connections produced an 11.8% wrong answer rate. Mosaic: 0%."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "a2f4a3cdb92a424ba50c94a244b4222c",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "When your VP of Content asks whether to spend $6 million renewing Night Market, an 11.8% chance of the AI hallucinating the retention math isn't an option. The model shouldn't be guessing what your business means. With Strategy Mosaic, it doesn't have to."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "_version": 1
          },
          "_metadata": {
            "uid": "cs5f25fbc3777bdeb2"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "section_anchor": {
          "header_text": "Frequently Asked Questions",
          "_metadata": {
            "uid": "cs2c9eafda80fad7bc"
          },
          "section_id": "frequently-asked-questions"
        }
      },
      {
        "accordion": {
          "accordion_item": [
            {
              "title": "What is a context layer?",
              "_metadata": {
                "uid": "cs0694e791058ae85b"
              },
              "content": {
                "type": "doc",
                "attrs": {},
                "uid": "29dd571eb17442499549e9cfce8b89bc",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "p",
                    "attrs": {},
                    "uid": "5b4fac92da3b45869d3ee1e56ec3ca07",
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "A context layer is the system that assembles business meaning at the moment a question is asked. It combines metadata, semantic definitions, relational structure, and live data so that AI can answer using your organization's actual business logic instead of guessing. Strategy Mosaic works as this layer, applying governed definitions before a query ever touches raw data."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "_version": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "title": "What's the difference between a semantic layer and a data catalog?",
              "_metadata": {
                "uid": "cs18e31d4c29b7f44f"
              },
              "content": {
                "type": "doc",
                "attrs": {},
                "uid": "3fba283fcddc408c9bbae7d3fc51fd82",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "p",
                    "attrs": {},
                    "uid": "a6b62ab439234385a5521dd5ee019833",
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "A data catalog documents that a field exists and describes its metadata — owner, refresh schedule, quality status. A semantic layer goes further by defining what that field means to the business and enforcing that definition consistently across every tool that uses it. Strategy Mosaic applies this distinction directly: cataloging tells you a metric exists, Mosaic makes sure everyone calculates it the same way."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "_version": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "title": "Do you need a semantic layer, an ontology, and a knowledge graph separately?",
              "_metadata": {
                "uid": "cs70e210045e4e802c"
              },
              "content": {
                "type": "doc",
                "attrs": {},
                "uid": "bb043f9e3f0a4d5a93f6a8491b1fa211",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "p",
                    "attrs": {},
                    "uid": "a43040982240400e9097ba4c97a4547d",
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "Not as five standalone products. Metadata, ontology, and knowledge graphs each describe or connect your data, but only a semantic layer settles what the business terms actually mean and applies that meaning consistently. Strategy Mosaic is built as the layer where those definitions live, so an answer means the same thing in every meeting regardless of which other systems supplied the underlying facts."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "_version": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "title": "Why does AI give inconsistent answers without a semantic layer?",
              "_metadata": {
                "uid": "csbfc7d5961efadebd"
              },
              "content": {
                "type": "doc",
                "attrs": {},
                "uid": "a41e4d24fd0349d58832893a9022a498",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "p",
                    "attrs": {},
                    "uid": "2c61b73d12d44469b9bc880ef6130273",
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "Without a governed semantic layer, an AI tool has to infer business logic on its own, and that inference changes depending on the prompt, the model, or the day. In head-to-head testing, direct LLM-to-database connections produced an 11.8% wrong answer rate, while Strategy Mosaic, which applies business definitions before a query runs rather than letting the model guess, produced 0%."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "_version": 1
              }
            }
          ],
          "_metadata": {
            "uid": "csb08d799678da95e5"
          },
          "accordion_options": "closed"
        }
      }
